HKUST(GZ) Connect licensing
===========================

This repository is a combined work with code from more than one provenance
line. It is not offered under a permissive license, and this file does not
relicense any upstream material.

1. GPL-covered components
-------------------------

The desktop application, CLI, project documentation, release tooling, and
other files outside `engine/` are licensed under GPL-3.0-only unless a file or
third-party notice says otherwise. They include work derived from
`heeh02/HKUST-GZ-Connect` at commit
`321cecdc860b96f25c36d99447b5f151bc18c7a2`, which was published under
GPL-3.0-only.

The complete GPL text is in `LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt`.

2. Engine combined terms
------------------------

The `engine/` component retains GPL-3.0-only obligations from the project
above. Its EasyConnect-compatible protocol implementation was also developed
after review of `Mythologyli/zju-connect` v1.1.1, which is AGPL-3.0-only.
Because this project cannot establish a reliable expression-level boundary
between those provenance lines, `engine/` is distributed conservatively under
the combined expression:

    GPL-3.0-only AND AGPL-3.0-only

GPLv3 section 13 and AGPLv3 section 13 permit GPLv3 and AGPLv3 covered works to
be combined while each license continues to govern its covered material and
the AGPL network-interaction requirements apply to the combination as stated
in those sections.

The complete AGPL text is in `LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt`.

3. Distribution as a whole
---------------------------

The packaged application and CLI include the engine. The distribution must
therefore be handled as a GPLv3/AGPLv3 combined work. Source recipients must
retain this file, both GNU license texts, `NOTICE.md`, `PROVENANCE.md`, and
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Third-party dependencies remain under their respective licenses. In
particular, the compiled userspace netstack is BSD-3-Clause and its required
copyright notice, license conditions, and disclaimer are reproduced in
`LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-GeiserX-tailscale-rs.txt` and
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

See `PROVENANCE.md` for exact versions and source relationships. This summary
is provided to make the repository's licensing boundaries explicit; the
license texts control if this summary conflicts with them.
